  "notes": "Cause code X (Other) governs category per official coding despite narrative describing a discrete component (gasket) failure; theme captures the vendor-equipment/temporary-modification angle. AGCS is a temporary modification system actively involved in the event (not mere design context) so it is modeled as a System node. Plant installed chillers explicitly realigned and returned ice bed to operable status, meeting the BACKED_UP_BY bar. The second isolation valve's failure to auto-close is modeled as a separate, parallel FailureMode triggered by the same low-low level signal, per an additional planned corrective action (work order to repair it) -- it did not itself drive the ice-bed-inoperable consequence chain, which proceeded via loss of cooling instead. No previous similar events were identified in the narrative, so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge was created."
